  :doc/body
  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 30

This is the first timed ranking of production count-loop against LLVM.
Iteration 29 ranked the same GMIR against the old all-vreg policy.
This file ranks it against rustc `-O3`. Encodings are not a ranking.

Two LLVM arms, one paper. The folded ceiling is not a call+loop ranking.
The shape-matched arm is. Both go through `kotoba-lang/perfgate`.
Neither seals. `:llvm-beaten` stays false.

Do not overwrite 04-29. Do not rematch `kernel_wide` (iteration 14).
Do not ship rust sources into amu.

## What was timed

amu arm reuses the iteration-29 production bytes. Same GMIR
(`call-and-back-edge-module`, export `count-loop`): acc=0, while n≠0
call `id(1)`, acc+=stepped, n-=1, return acc. Oracle n=50 → 50.

| arm | what ran | sha256 |
|---|---|---|
| amu | iter-29 `prod.bin` `:call-live`, 92 B, offset **4** | `d420fd28183a74f36c10728b80e6d7f744ff0bb6dddb7ff70efc47060e346f73` |
| llvm (ceiling) | rustc `-O3` `count_loop`, identity `id` inlinable | `9c88737d95f109af7d11e83a0b53f08709dff26c77c6551d139079d751fd918e` |
| llvm-call (shape) | rustc `-O3` `count_loop_call`, `#[inline(never)]` + `black_box` | `d8f626606e24c91cc16566533393504ae7b118e6290bc7faa81829e83e3a8bf3` |

`id` sits at offset 0 (4-byte `ret`). Offset 4 is the count-loop export.

LLVM binaries were compiled on this Air (`rustc 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14)`,
`--edition 2021 -C opt-level=3 -C codegen-units=1`, aarch64-apple-darwin)
because judah has no rustc. Timing ran on **judah**. This Air is not a
ranking host.

## The ceiling is a mov

`count_loop.s` timed loop `LBB6_3` stores and loads `n` (`black_box`) and
compares the outer call counter. There is no `bl` to `id`, no add, no
inner `subs`. LLVM proved `count_loop(n)==n` and deleted the work.
Local one-shot result 50 is real; the work is gone. min 0.605 ns is the
same band as iteration-14 LLVM identity (0.605 ns). Ranking amu 39 ns
against this is ranking a loop+call against a mov.

`#[inline(never)]` on `id` was not enough. The first `count_loop_call.s`
was identical to the ceiling: IPO still saw identity. `black_box` on
`id`'s result and on `acc` is what kept the loop. Verified: symbol
`__RNv…count_loop_call2id`, inner `LBB7_9` does `bl id`, add, `subs`,
`b.ne`. That arm is the actual call+loop ranking.

Do not chase the folded ceiling with allocator or isel.

## Oracle

Harness `warmup=0` and `n=0` are outside the admitted range. One-shot
used 1 call and 1 warmup. Result **50** on all three arms, no
`KEXE_TRAP`. The same result held on every scored sample.

## Times

12 discarded frequency-warmup rotations (three arms rotated), then 25
scored rotated samples. Judge: **min ns/call** reported; **perfgate
uses means**.

judah loadavg `{ 1.60 1.63 1.68 }` start and end. load1 stayed under 4.

| arm | min | mean | median | p95 | max | rel stdev |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| amu (`:call-live`) | 38.74 | 38.848 | 38.81 | 39.11 | 39.29 | 0.0033 |
| llvm (folded) | 0.605 | 0.611 | 0.607 | 0.647 | 0.648 | 0.0199 |
| llvm-call (shape) | 36.782 | 37.129 | 37.093 | 37.698 | 38.183 | 0.0084 |

min ratio amu/folded **64.03×**. mean ratio **63.55×**.
min ratio amu/llvm-call **1.053×**. mean ratio **1.046×**.
mean improvement vs llvm-call **-4.63%**.

Dump: `/tmp/iter30-dump/` on judah and the workstation (`count_loop`,
`count_loop_call`, `*.s`, `*.rs`, `rank.py`, `samples.json`, `arms.edn`,
`qualify.edn`). amu bytes remain `/tmp/iter29-dump/prod.bin`. Runner:
`/tmp/kexe-benchmark-iter29`.

## perfgate

`perfgate.core/qualify` twice on the 25 ns/call vectors. Candidate =
amu, metric `:wall-ns`, unit `\"ns/call\"`. Machine descriptor
`:measured` from the same judah sysctl as iteration 29 (ncpu 10,
pagesize 16384, cachelinesize 128, l1d 65536, l2 4194304, brand Apple
M4). ways not reported; not fabricated. perfgate `d4417d77`, machine
`4f57144a`.

### Ceiling (baseline = folded LLVM)

- mean improvement **-62.55** (required +0.05)
- gap **38.236 ns** > summed stdev **0.141 ns** (separated)
- `:improvement-below-threshold`
- `:qualified? false`
- **no claim artifact**

Correct refusal. This arm is not a call+loop. Do not write 64× into
`amu/docs/performance.md`.

### Shape-matched (baseline = llvm-call)

- mean improvement **-4.63%** (amu slower)
- gap **1.718 ns** > summed stdev **0.439 ns** (separated from noise)
- relative stdev 0.0033 / 0.0084 (allowed 0.10)
- `:improvement-below-threshold` (required +5%)
- `:qualified? false`
- **no claim artifact**

The arms are apart. The gap is smaller than the gate. Do not claim
amu beats LLVM. Do not claim LLVM beats amu. Do not write 1.053× into
`amu/docs/performance.md`.

`:llvm-beaten` remains false. The leaf ranking (iteration 14) stays
refused. Do not rematch leaf vs LLVM.

